Methodology/Pipeline
Dataintegration(GCDD+Mindat+MRDS+MED)
│
▼
Cleaning・harmonisation・featureengineering
│
├─►RQ1:Diagnosticfeatures—PCA,RandomForestimportance,
│ one-wayANOVA,Kruskal–Wallis,Chi-square(α=0.05,η²effectsizes)
│
├─►RQ2:Classification—RandomForest (500trees),XGBoost,SVM(RBF)
│ stratified80/20split・10-foldCV・SpatialStripSplitting
│ metrics:Accuracy,Precision,Recall,F1,MCC・SHAPinterpretation
│ target:>85% held-outaccuracy, McNemar testvs.expertmethods
│
├─►RQ3:Patterndiscovery—Apriori association rules
│ (support≥0.05,confidence≥0.70,lift > 2.0),
│ co-occurrencenetworkanalysis,Pearson/Spearmangradecorrelations
│
└─►RQ4:Spatio-temporalanalysis—Moran'sI&LISAhotspots,

KernelDensityEstimationheatmaps,DBSCANbeltdelineation,
metallogenicage-frequencyanalysisvs.geodynamicevents

KeyFeatures
• Statisticallyvalidateddiagnosticfeaturesforfivecopperdeposittypes
• InterpretableMLclassifiers(RF/XGBoost/SVM)withspatiallyrobustvalidationand
SHAPexplainability
• Association-ruleandnetworkminingofmineral–geochemicalco-occurrences
• Globalheatmaps,metallogenic-beltdelineation,andexplorationtargetingrecommen
dations
• Reproduciblepipeline: versionedcode,fixedrandomseeds,documentedenvironment
RepositoryStructure
├── data/ #rawandprocessed datasets(see data/READMEforaccessnotes)
├── notebooks/ #exploratoryanalysisandfigures
├── src/
│ ├──preprocessing/ #data integration,cleaning,featureengineering
│ ├──features/ #RQ1diagnostic-featureanalysis
│ ├──models/ #RQ2classifiers,training,evaluation
│ ├──patterns/ #RQ3association rules and network analysis
│ └──spatial/ #RQ4spatialstatisticsandmapping
├── results/ #figures,tables,trainedmodelartefacts
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md

Installation

git clonehttps://github.com/mpshalwindi/global-copper-deposit-analysis.git
cdglobal-copper-deposit-analysis
python-mvenv.venv&&source .venv/bin/activate #Windows:.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install-rrequirements.txt
Core dependencies: pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, xgboost, scipy, mlxtend (Apriori), networkx,
esda/pysal,geopandas,shap,matplotlib,seaborn,openmindat(MindatAPIclient).

Usage
# 1.Buildtheintegrateddataset(downloads GCDD; queries MindatAPI+MRDS)
pythonsrc/preprocessing/build_dataset.py
# 2.Runeachresearch-questionmodule
pythonsrc/features/diagnostic_features.py #RQ1
pythonsrc/models/train_classifiers.py #RQ2
pythonsrc/patterns/association_mining.py #RQ3
pythonsrc/spatial/spatiotemporal_analysis.py #RQ4
Outputs(figures,tables,modelartefacts)arewrittentoresults/.

Results
Tobeupdatedasanalysisprogresses.Plannedoutputsinclude:

• Ranked diagnostic-feature table with statistical validation (RQ1)
• Classifier comparison and confusion-matrix evaluation vs. traditional methods (RQ2)
• High-lift association rules and co-occurrence network maps (RQ3)
• Global deposit-density heatmaps and under-explored-region recommendations (RQ4)
Ethical Considerations
• Open-access data only — GCDD, Mindat, USGS-MRDS, and MED; no personal or proprietary
data.
• Transparency and reproducibility — full pipeline is documented and version-controlled.
• Attribution — all data sources are credited; licences respected (Mindat data accessed via its API
under its terms of use; not redistributed).
• Responsible interpretation — model outputs support, not replace, expert geological judgement.
Roadmap
• Data integration and harmonisation pipeline
• RQ1diagnostic-feature validation
• RQ2classifier benchmark (> 85% target, SSS validation)
• RQ3association-rule and network outputs
• RQ4global heatmaps and targeting recommendations
• Deployable classification module

